;;; core.effective -- effective homology as one library: reductions and the
;;; basic perturbation lemma, discrete vector fields, objects with effective
;;; homology (products, twisted products, classifying spaces, K(pi, n)), the
;;; Whitehead tower and homotopy groups, hypercovers and descent.
;;;
;;; Usage: (require core.effective)
;;;
;;; Loads the whole facility (each part can also be required alone):
;;;   core.effective.chain         linear combinations, locally effective
;;;                                complexes, reductions and their identities
;;;   core.effective.perturbation  the basic perturbation lemma, vector-field
;;;                                reductions, collapse matchings, tensor
;;;                                products and bar constructions of reductions
;;;   core.effective.simplicial    normalized chains, Eilenberg-Zilber (vector
;;;                                field and AW / EML / SHI), simplicial groups,
;;;                                twisted products, W-bar G, K(Z, n), K(Z/m, n)
;;;   core.effective.homotopy      cocycles as maps into K(pi, n), principal
;;;                                fibrations, the Whitehead tower, pi_n
;;;   core.effective.hypercover    hypercovers of finite spaces by cones, Cech
;;;                                nerves, mapping spaces into 2-types and
;;;                                3-types on both sides of a cover
;;;
;;; Reference: docs/reference/stdlib/effective.md; design: ADR-0038
;;; (docs/design/adr/0038-effective-homology.md).
;;; Sources: F. Sergeraert, J. Rubio, "Constructive algebraic topology",
;;; Bull. Sci. Math. 126 (2002); the Kenzo program (X. Dousson, J. Rubio,
;;; F. Sergeraert, Y. Siret); A. Romero, F. Sergeraert, "Discrete vector
;;; fields and fundamental algebraic topology", arXiv:1005.5685 (2010).

(require core.effective.chain)
(require core.effective.perturbation)
(require core.effective.simplicial)
(require core.effective.homotopy)
(require core.effective.hypercover)
